# Settings > About radio, once the client has asked what firmware exists for the board.
#
# Three of the four answers, because the fourth - "checking" - is the one that costs a frame
# and says nothing: it is the indeterminate meter, and gauges.scene already films one of those.
# What is worth looking at here is the pair of rows: what the check found, and why it cannot be
# acted on. They are different answers and they sit next to each other, so a picture is the
# only way to see whether that reads as one thought or as two.
scene demo
clock 2026-09-09 14:20
delay 1800
config

tab settings
key down 1
key a

# Behind, on the bus that would carry it: nothing refuses this except the phase that installs
# firmware not being written yet, which is what the last row has to say without reading as a
# button somebody forgot to wire up.
firmware behind
hold 2400

# The same board on the other bus. This is the refusal worth having - it names something the
# user can go and do - and the row above it has not changed, which is the point of the two
# being separate rows.
firmware behind usb
hold 2400

# A model four boards share. Upstream's own flasher picks the first; this one says so and stops.
firmware behind ambiguous
hold 2400

# And the settled case, where the only row left is the version.
firmware current
hold 2400

# The channel above them, which decides which of upstream's two release lists the press below
# it reads. Switching drops the answer - it belonged to the other question - so the row under
# it goes back to "not checked" until a check runs again.
firmware-channel alpha
hold 2400
